  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets a 7% permanent failure cap (above the 5% benchmark) with a 5% corrective-action trigger and up to 24 months of supervised sales. S5 mandates recall at 8/100k but explicitly not a permanent ban, with prompt notices and no serious-injury clause. S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 24 months and retrofit to 72 months, while S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months."
 },
